########################################################################
## Renderer defaults for the visual regression suite.
##
## This file exists because the suite used to inherit its defaults from
## openrender/.orenderrc -- the deploy tree, which is gitignored and only
## populated by `cmake --install`. On a fresh clone that file is absent, so
## every scene rendered with different defaults than its reference image was
## produced with, and the entire suite failed. Measured against the scenes as
## they stand: 47 of 206 declare no Format and 155 declare no PixelSamples, so
## the values below are load-bearing, not cosmetic.
##
## It is deliberately hermetic: no %ORENDERHOME% or /usr/local entries, so a
## stray /usr/local/shaders on a developer's machine cannot change a result.
## Search paths resolve only through the environment variables the test harness
## sets, all of which point inside the source or build tree.
##
## Keep Format and PixelSamples in step with the reference images. Changing
## either invalidates every reference for a scene that does not set its own.
########################################################################

Option "shaderformat" "default"  ["rslo"]

Option "searchpath" "shader"     ["&:.:%SHADERS%"]
Option "searchpath" "texture"    ["&:.:%TEXTURES%"]
Option "searchpath" "archive"    ["&:.:%RIBS%"]
Option "searchpath" "display"    ["&:.:%DISPLAYS%"]
Option "searchpath" "procedural" ["&:.:%PROCEDURALS%"]
Option "searchpath" "geometry"   ["&:.:%GEOMETRIES%"]

Format 640 480 1
PixelSamples 2 2
